  "summary": "The code contained a critical RCE vulnerability due to unsafe YAML deserialization and lacked essential production-grade safeguards like error handling and input size limits. The refactored code implements safe parsing, type safety, and robust error handling to ensure stability and security.",
  "fixed_code": "import yaml\nfrom flask import Flask, jsonify, request, abort\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\napp.config['MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH'] = 1 * 1024 * 1024  # Limit to 1MB\n\ndef parse_pipeline(raw_text: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Parses a YAML pipeline specification string into a dictionary.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        data = yaml.safe_load(raw_text)\n        return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n    except yaml.YAMLError:\n        return {}\n\n@app.route(\"/pipelines/validate\", methods=[\"POST\"])\ndef validate_pipeline():\n    if not request.data:\n        abort(400, description=\"Empty request body\")\n    \n    spec = parse_pipeline(request.get_data(as_text=True))\n    steps = spec.get(\"steps\", []) if spec else []\n    return jsonify(valid=bool(steps), step_count=len(steps))"
